From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Kane <kanej1973@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 20:36:17 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 06/14] [VectraOS] no Float80 on VectraOS

Swift on VectraOS has no Float80 (decided 2026-10-11), so that a program
means the same on its three machines: arm64 and riscv64 can't have it,
and x86_64's would need a long double libm. CLongDouble isn't defined;
long double stays C's (VectraOS's libc has strtold and printf's %L).
